PATIENT VIGNETTE
A 12-year-old girl is brought to the ED by her parents after falling off her bicycle. She was not wearing a helmet and hit her head on the pavement. The girl is conscious and answering questions but complains of a severe headache and nausea. Her parents report that she was unconscious for about 30 seconds after the fall. Vital signs: BP 108/72, HR 90, RR 18. No other injuries are noted, and there is no vomiting.

